# The REBOL 3 interpreter used to check JEBOL's answers against a real one.
#
# A tool rather than source, and a 2.1M platform-specific binary at that.
# Fetch your own from the Oldes/Rebol3 releases, picking the build for your
# machine; see docs/allium-checker-notes.md for which asset and how to run
# it. The binaries linked from rebol.com are i386 and will not run on any
# current macOS.
/r3
/r3.exe

# The same interpreter, built from the source in rebol3-source/ rather than
# downloaded, by `scripts/build-r3.sh`. It is the one to ask, because a release
# is always older than the checkout beside it and the two do disagree. The
# downloaded /r3 is still needed: Rebol's pre-make step is a Rebol script, so
# the old binary is what builds the new one. Its generated spec lands in
# build/r3/, which the Gradle line further down already covers.
/r3-head

# Rebol's own source, symlinked in so the IDE indexes it and the MCP can search
# it. It is the authority every port is read from -- `src/core/*.c`, `boot/*.reb`,
# `src/tests/units/*.r3` -- and keeping it outside the project meant every search
# of it fell back to grep.
#
# A link rather than a copy, so there is one checkout on disk and it updates with
# its own git. Never committed: it is 25,000 lines of somebody else's Apache-2.0
# code, and vendoring it would put JEBOL's own history and licensing in doubt.
#
# Make your own with:
#     ln -s ~/Code/personal/rebol3-source rebol3-source
/rebol3-source

# Gradle
/.gradle/
/build/

# The Allium CLI's one-time notice marker, when the cache directory is not
# writable and it falls back to the project root.
/.allium-cli-notice-shown

# Editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
